ct zero, uniqueness, Newton convergence from an arbitrary seed, or a discretization error bound.\n\nEach step solves a coupled block system with $d+m$ unknowns. At most $B$ Newton corrections and $B+1$ Newton residual evaluations are made per attempted step, plus at most one residual reevaluation to record the unscaled blocks after a root status. Each correction uses one solve with the current $(d+m)$-dimensional block Jacobian. Work per residual, Jacobian assembly, and linear solve depends on the backend.",
